<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <div class="content-body">
        <h3 class="subsection-title">Mental Illness Awareness Week</h3>
        <p>October 3-9</p>
        <p>This year's NAMI Mental Illness Awareness Week theme is "Together for Mental Health." One common influence on mental health is stress. Stress is the result of pressures or challenges that we face in our lives. Stress can cause feelings of unease, anxiety, frustration, nervousness, and more. Stress can also cause physical symptoms, such as headaches, stomachaches, or fatigue. Feeling stressed is normal, especially during a crisis. You can learn more about stress and how to manage it by visiting <span data-field="mental_health.website">{{ mental_health.website }}</span>.</p>
        <p>What you can do:</p>
        <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
          <li>Take five. Take a deep breath and relax. Even five minutes can help.</li>
          <li>Take a walk, stretch, or attend a virtual exercise class.</li>
          <li>Talk to someone you trust. A friend, family member, or a professional.</li>
          <li>Create a daily routine that includes rest, exercise, and relaxation.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>For additional resources on mental health and coping with stress, visit the <span data-field="mental_health.resource_link">{{ mental_health.resource_link }}</span>. For more information on NAMI, visit <span data-field="mental_health.nami_link">{{ mental_health.nami_link }}</span>. Explore the Nature Center's calendar of events for free, accessible, and engaging activities this week and all year long!</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_6.jpg" alt="Mental Health Image" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
