    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <div class="content-body">
        <h3 class="subsection-title">Sustainability Month</h3>
        <p>Jamie Greiner</p>
        <p>October is Campus Sustainability Month. This year, UMU's theme is "The 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development," adopted by all United Nations Member States in 2015, provides a shared blueprint for peace and prosperity for people and the planet. It is a universal call to action on climate change, social equity, and economic development. Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), which are an urgent call for action by all countries in a global partnership. They recognize that ending poverty and hunger, improving health and education, reducing inequality, and spurring economic growth—all while tackling climate change and protecting our oceans and forests—is possible.</p>
        <p>These goals seem daunting and out of reach for the average person, but it's changing this exact mindset that will ultimately help us achieve them. The first step is to educate ourselves about the goals and then tell people about them. We can all contribute to their achievement. The first step is to educate ourselves about the goals and then tell people about them. We can all contribute to their achievement.</p>
        <p>Think simple to start - plant a tree, participate in a clean-up event, reduce your consumption (energy, water, food), reuse bags, bottles, mugs, etc.), donate, borrow instead of buying, volunteer, write your representatives about environmental and social justice issues, plant wildflowers, and support local businesses. Every action counts!</p>
        <p>Lastly, enjoy and appreciate the natural world that is all around you. The more clearly we can focus our attention on the wonders and realities of the universe about us, the less taste we shall have for destruction - Rachel Carson (author of Silent Spring).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_7.jpg" alt="Sustainability Image" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

